    "category": "security",
    "evidence": "Probe /tmp/uri_review_R36/full.py, text 'Claim your energy rebate refund at {} before the deadline.': 'refunds-portal.|0|/claim' -> has_link_or_contact False; verify() keeps the cited sentence; extractive() selects it; surface.clean() shows it unmasked; validate._URLISH no match. Same for 'refunds-portal.0||0/claim', 'refunds-portal.|0|' and 'refunds-portal ~ |0|'. Control 'refunds-portal.l0l/claim' -> detected, dropped, shown as '[link removed]'. Cause: `if run.lower() not in _ALL_TLDS and any(ch.isalpha() for ch in run)` (comment 'numbers (000) never') skips runs with no letter even when they contain '|', which is not a digit; then 'letters < 2' returns the run unchanged. confusables_ascii lists '|'->'l' and '0'->'o'. Sweep /tmp/uri_review_R36/sweep3.py: every context tried (real dot, ' . ', '[.]', ' ~ ', U+4E36 separator, path) misses '|0|', '10|', '|01', '0|10', '01|0', '0||0'.",
    "files": [
     "uri_web/untrusted.py:810",
     "uri_web/untrusted.py:794",
     "uri_web/untrusted.py:836",
     "uri_web/surface.py:38",
     "uri_a2ui/validate.py:150"
    ],
    "id": "R36-01",
    "owner_decision": false,
    "severity": "HIGH",
    "suggested_fix": "In _ascii_variant, treat as a number only a run made entirely of digits (run.isdigit()); fold any run that contains '|' or mixes '|' with digits, in both the ending-reading and the general fold. Add regression cases for '.|0|', '.0||0', '.10|', '~ |0|'.",
    "title": "R31-01/D29 class still open: a top-level domain spelt only with ASCII look-alikes that include '|' ('refunds-portal.|0|/claim' = .lol, '.0||0' = .ollo) is never folded because _ascii_variant needs an alphabetic character in the run, so it passes has_link_or_contact, mask_links, verify(), extractive(), the research surface and the A2UI validator (W1-AC12/AC15)"
   }
